o another account, HiraṇyaKaśipu himself angrily kicked the pillar to convince his son of the absurdity of his faith), when Viṣṇu came out half-man and half-lion, and tore HiraṇyaKaśipu to pieces. Prahlāda succeeded his father, and reigned wisely and righteously.]"}]},{"n":5,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रह्रा [prahrā] ह्ला [hlā] दन [dana], (ह्ला) दन a. Gladdening, delighting; प्रह्लादनं ज्योतिरजन्यनेन "},{"t":"cite","s":"R.13.4","q":"R"},{"t":"txt","s":". -नम् Causing joy or delight, gladdening, delighting; यथा प्रह्लादनाच्चन्द्रः "},{"t":"cite","s":"R.4.12","q":"R"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]}]}],"prahrasaH":[{"id":"prahrAsaH","headword":"प्रह्रासः","headword_slp1":"prahrAsaH","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रह्रासः [prahrāsḥ], 1 Diminution, decrease."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Languishing, fading away."}]}]}],"prahlana":[{"id":"prahlanna","headword":"प्रह्लन्न","headword_slp1":"prahlanna","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रह्लन्न [prahlanna], p. p. Delighted, joyful, pleased."}]}]}],"prahlaniH":[{"id":"prahlanniH","headword":"प्रह्लन्निः","headword_slp1":"prahlanniH","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रह्लन्निः [prahlanniḥ], f. Pleasure, delight; also प्रह्लत्तिः "},{"t":"sutra","s":"P.VI. 4.95","id":"6.4.95"},{"t":"txt","s":" com."}]}]}],"prahladaka":[{"id":"prahlAdaka","headword":"प्रह्लादक","headword_slp1":"prahlAdaka","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रह्लादक [prahlādaka], a. Causing pleasure, refreshing."}]}]}],"prahlad":[{"id":"prahlAd","headword":"प्रह्लाद्","headword_slp1":"prahlAd","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रह्लाद् [prahlād], 1 Ā. To be greatly delighted, rejoice. -Caus. To delight, exhilarate, gladden."}]}]}],"prahva":[{"id":"prahva","headword":"प्रह्व","headword_slp1":"prahva","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रह्व [prahva], a."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Sloping, slanting, inclined; प्रह्वानतीव क्वचिदु- द्धतिश्रितः Śi.12.56."}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Sto